# Task: report whether an Arch package is installed.
# Program: this file.
# Run: execute docs/recipes/desktop-pacman-query.program --input package=vim
# Test with fakes: put a fake `pacman` earlier on PATH. Make it exit 0 for `-Q vim` and
#   exit 1 for `-Q nosuchpkg`; expect "installed" and "not installed" lines.
# Explain: pacman's own version line goes straight to stdout; the program adds one line.
# Replaces (Bash): pacman -Q "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo installed || echo not installed
accept package as text
run "pacman" with arguments ["-Q", package] and keep status as code
if code is 0
  run "printf" with arguments ["%s is installed\n", package]
otherwise
  run "printf" with arguments ["%s is not installed\n", package]
